    "title": "Young tennis players set to compete in Mobile for national championship - NewsBreak",
    "text": "By Jonathan Myers ,\n1 hours ago\nMOBILE, Ala. ( WKRG ) — For the 15th year, the Mobile Tennis Center is hosting the USTA Boys’ 12s and 14s National Championship.\nHistoric Oakleigh House Museum in Mobile closes for major repairs: what to know The championship is being held from Saturday, August 8th to Saturday, August 15th at the largest public tennis facility in the United States. Admission to watch the competition is free.\nCherish Lombard was joined on “The 4 on 5” by Scott Novak, general manager of the Mobile Tennis Center and Sami Udell, director of tennis and tournament promotion to discuss this annual championship’s impact on the Port City.\nCopyright 2026 Nexstar Media, Inc. All rights reserved. This material may not be published, broadcast, rewritten, or redistributed. For the latest news, weather, sports, and streaming video, head to WKRG News 5.",
    "summary": "MOBILE, Ala. ( WKRG ) — For the 15th year, the Mobile Tennis Center is hosting the USTA Boys’ 12s and 14s National Championship. Historic Oakleigh House Museum in Mobile closes for major repairs: what to know The championship is being held from Saturday, August 8th to Saturday, August 15th at the largest public tennis facility in the United States. Cherish Lombard was joined on “The 4 on 5” by Scott Novak, general manager of the Mobile Tennis Center and Sami Udell, director of tennis and tournament promotion to discuss this annual championship’s impact on the Port City.",
